/-!
# Atlas V-03 (block A): every compatible real frame tangent is the tangent of a real normalised family

Given a background null frame `(g₀, gi₀, E₀, Θ₀)` on an open `U` whose frame has the real pattern
`e_{swap23 A} = conj e_A` (`l`, `n` real, `m̄ = conj m`), a field `F₀`, and a real tangent `(h, f, B)` with
`B` of the same pattern and the first-order normalisation `FrameCompat g₀ h E₀ B U`, the **realisation family**

* `T_ε = E₀ + ε B` (`rzE`), `Θ_ε = T_ε⁻¹` (`rzTh`), on `W = {(ε, y) | y ∈ U, det T_ε(y) ≠ 0}` (`rzW`),
* `G_ε = Θ_εᵀ η Θ_ε` (`rzGc`), `GI_ε = T_ε η T_εᵀ` (`rzGIc`) — proved **real** (`im = 0`) from the pattern, and the
  real metric / inverse are their real parts (`rzG`, `rzGI`),
* `F_ε = F₀ + ε f` (`rzF`)

is an `NPFamily` (true inverse, exact null Gram matrix on every slice, joint `C^∞`) whose tangent at `ε = 0` is exactly
`(h, f, B)` (`realize`). It is a kinematic realisation only: no `ε ≠ 0` member is claimed to solve any field equation.
Outside `U` the definitions fall back to the background (so that `ε = 0` gives the background as functions); only
