/-!
# Atlas V-03 (block C2'): regularity of the tangent and of its NP variations; KN realisation; complex tangents

* `contDiffOn_var_of`: a function that is, at every point of the open slice `ε = 0`, the genuine `ε`-derivative of a
  jointly `C^∞` family is `C^∞` on the slice (`contDiffOn_deriv_slice` + uniqueness of derivatives).
* Hence, for every `NPFamily`/`NPTangent`: `h` and all NP variation functions (`weylFVar`, `omLVar`, `ricFVar`,
  `FfrFVar`, `HfrVar`, `JfrVar`; at KN also `srcS1 … srcS4`) are `C^∞` on the slice. These are theorems, not
  hypotheses.
* `NullFrameData.restrict`, `knRealize`: every compatible real tangent `(h, f, B)` on an open `U ⊆ domReg` (KN
  background, `RealFrameTangent`) is the genuine tangent of a `KNFam` whose slice is exactly `U` (via `realize`;
  kinematic only: the family is **not** required to solve the field equations).
* `RealFrameTangent.lcomb`: compatible real tangents form a real vector space.
* `KNCTan`: a complex tangent `τ = τ_R + i τ_I` whose two real parts are compatible real tangents on `U`; closed
  under complex scalar multiplication and addition (`KNCTan.smul`, `KNCTan.add`). -/

